        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 21, \"total_count\": 21, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"New Resume\\\" opened editor titled \\\"Untitled Resume\\\"; contact inputs all value:\\\"\\\", summary \\\"\\\" (0/500), experience & education lists empty, skills empty-message shown. All fields immediately editable.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Template tab lists Modern/Classic/Minimal. Selecting Classic then Minimal moved data-semtag-state=\\\"selected\\\" correctly and re-rendered the preview in distinct layouts (Classic: uppercase headings, position/date/company order; Minimal: uppercase contact line, date-column layout). All contact, summary, 2 experience, education and skills content remained present in every style.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Contact 6 fields filled & persisted; summary text saved (69/500); 2 experience entries added/edited, move-up reordered them (Babbage Works now first) with values intact; education entry added, edited, second entry removed leaving first intact; skills added, level changed Intermediate→Expert, skill removed successfully.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sections tab exposes order (move-up/down) and visibility toggle per section. Moving Skills up changed editor order to contact,summary,experience,skills,education and the preview re-rendered with SKILLS before EDUCATION. Hiding Education removed its heading and \\\"University of London\\\" from the preview; re-showing restored it in the new position.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Toggle labelled \\\"Hide Preview\\\" removed preview.document from the DOM and became \\\"Show Preview\\\"; editor fields intact (company still \\\"Analytical Engines Ltd\\\"). Clicking again restored the preview with all content (name, experience, education, skills, custom \\\"About Me\\\" heading) and the previously selected Classic template still marked selected.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Card menu > Duplicate created \\\"Ada Data Scientist Resume (Copy)\\\" carrying all source content. Renamed it via the rename dialog to \\\"Ada ML Engineer Resume\\\". Edited the copy (name→Ada L. Byron, email→ada.ml@example.com, new summary); reopening the source showed it unchanged (Ada Lovelace / ada@example.com / original summary).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"During one session created \\\"Ada Data Scientist Resume\\\" (Classic), duplicated+renamed it to \\\"Ada ML Engineer Resume\\\" (Classic, independently edited content), and created \\\"Ada Product Manager Resume\\\" (Modern, own contact name \\\"Ada PM\\\"). All 3 coexist alongside the 3 seeded resumes on the dashboard with distinct titles, templates and content, each reopenable and manageable via card menu (rename/duplicate/delete).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"ADA ml\\\" matched \\\"Ada ML Engineer Resume\\\" and \\\"mArKeTiNg\\\" matched \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\" — case-insensitive. Clearing the search restored all 6 resumes. Sort \\\"Oldest First\\\" gave Software Engineer, Marketing Manager, Product Designer, Ada Data Scientist, Ada ML Engineer, Ada Product Manager; \\\"Newest First\\\" gave the exact reverse — correct creation-date ordering both ways.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Creation-date filtering feature not implemented\", \"actual\": \"The dashboard offers no way to narrow resumes by creation date. Full snapshot (including hidden elements) exposes only dashboard.create, dashboard.search (text) and dashboard.sort (newest/oldest/title-asc/title-desc). A raw DOM scan found exactly one input on the page — the text search (type=\\\"text\\\") — no input[type=date], no date-range picker, no calendar, and no button/combobox matching /date|filter|from|to|range|created|between/ (only \\\"New Resume\\\" and \\\"Newest First\\\" buttons exist). Using the search box as a fallback with the exact displayed date \\\"Feb 25, 2024\\\" returned 0 results and the empty-state message. Therefore neither an exact creation date nor a date range can be applied, and no date criterion exists to clear.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing date-period validation: reversed and future periods accepted with no feedback\", \"actual\": \"On experience entry \\\"Analytical Engines Ltd\\\": set start=2020-01, end=2019-05 (end before start) — accepted, no error text in the entry (innerText shows only field labels), aria-invalid=null, validationMessage=\\\"\\\". Then set start=2030-01, end=2031-05 (both future; today 2026-08-27) — also accepted; inputs have no max attribute and the preview rendered \\\"Jan 2030 - May 2031\\\". No rejection or feedback in either case.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Experience & education start/end inputs are all input[type=month] (consistent MM/YYYY). Toggling \\\"I currently work here\\\" on entry 3opslrmjgah set end-date value=\\\"\\\" and disabled=true.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all resume changes are lost on reload; app resets to seeded demo data\", \"actual\": \"Before reload the dashboard held 5 resumes: \\\"Ada ML Engineer Resume\\\", \\\"Ada Data Scientist Resume\\\" (created, edited, duplicated and renamed during the session) plus 3 seeded ones, with \\\"Ada Product Manager Resume\\\" deleted. After reloading http://localhost:7005/ the dashboard showed only the 3 original seeded resumes (resume-1/2/3) — every created, edited, duplicated and renamed version was gone. Deletion also does not persist: deleted seeded \\\"Product Designer Resume\\\" (resume-3), reloaded, and it reappeared unchanged (\\\"Updated Feb 25, 2024\\\", Minimal). localStorage is empty (Object.keys(localStorage) = []), confirming state is in-memory only.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Dashboard rename dialog accepts a whitespace-only title, blanking the resume name; editor rename rejects it but gives no feedback\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard path (primary defect): card menu > Rename > entered \\\"   \\\" > Save. The dialog closed and the rename was COMMITTED — the resume card now renders an empty title (dashboard.resumes item sg8053e15n has name:\\\"\\\" where it was \\\"Ada Data Scientist Resume (Copy)\\\"). No validation blocked it and no error was shown. Editor path: entering \\\"   \\\" or \\\"\\\" in editor.title.input reverted to the prior title (title preserved) but displayed no validation feedback at all (no error text, no [role=alert]/toast/aria-live).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing \\\"Cambridge, UK\\\" into editor.contact.location updated preview.contact.location instantly (no save/refresh). Earlier, all 6 contact fields and summary text propagated to the preview on entry, and template switches (Modern→Classic→Minimal) re-rendered the preview immediately.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Moving Skills up re-rendered the preview immediately (SKILLS before EDUCATION) and toggling Education visibility off/on immediately removed/restored it. The layout persisted while navigating: after switching tabs, and after returning to the dashboard and reopening the resume, editor order remained contact,summary,experience,skills,education and the preview still showed Core Competencies before Academic Background.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edits were retained automatically with no explicit save: moving between Contact/Summary/Experience/Education/Skills/Template/Sections tabs preserved values; after clicking back to dashboard and reopening the card, title and all content persisted. Dashboard card showed \\\"Updated Aug 27, 2026\\\" (today) reflecting the update.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"In the selected style the preview rendered all visible populated sections: name, email, phone, location, linkedin, website, summary, both experience entries, education, and both skills (all 12 checks true). With a ~700-char description forcing a 625px-tall document, the preview panel has an overflow-y:scroll container and the page scrolls (scrollHeight 1130 > viewport 720); after scrolling, the document bottom was in view and the final section (\\\"ACADEMIC BACKGROUND ... Sep 2014 – Jun 2017\\\") was readable.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After switching editor tabs, returning to dashboard and reopening: all 6 contact fields intact (Ada Lovelace / ada@example.com / 555-0101 / Cambridge, UK / linkedin.com/in/ada / ada.dev), summary text, both experience entries (Babbage Works, Analytical Engines Ltd), education (University of London, GPA 3.9) and both skills (Mathematics, Logic Design) all still rendered.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Copy→original: edited copy (name, email, summary \\\"Machine learning engineer...\\\") — original still showed Ada Lovelace / ada@example.com / \\\"analytical engines\\\" summary, no copy text present. Original→copy: changed original phone to 555-9999 — reopened copy still had phone 555-0101, its own name/email/summary intact, and no trace of 555-9999. Independent in both directions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed via editor title to \\\"Ada Data Scientist Resume\\\"; editor.title observable shows that value, and the dashboard card (dashboard.resumes.item.z00f0xyp0g) displays the identical non-empty title \\\"Ada Data Scientist Resume\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Customized Summary section heading is not rendered in the Minimal style\", \"actual\": \"Section headings were customized to \\\"About Me\\\" (summary), \\\"Professional Experience\\\", \\\"Academic Background\\\", \\\"Core Competencies\\\". Modern and Classic render all four. Minimal renders \\\"PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\\\", \\\"ACADEMIC BACKGROUND\\\" and \\\"CORE COMPETENCIES\\\" but shows NO heading for the summary section — the summary text appears directly after the contact block (\\\"...ADA.DEV | EXPERIENCED MATHEMATICIAN AND ENGINEER...\\\"), so the custom \\\"About Me\\\" heading is missing even though the summary section is visible and has content.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
