__EVENT__ {
  "type": "message",
  "stage": "defect_detection",
  "status": null,
  "message": null,
  "payload": {
    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 21 checklist items have been tested and recorded — **16 PASS, 5 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe core resume-building experience is solid: creation, editing of all content types, template switching, section reordering/visibility, live preview, duplication with true data independence, and case-insensitive search with date sorting all work correctly.\n\n**Five defects found:**\n\n| ID | Issue |\n|---|---|\n| **CS-11** | **No persistence at all.** `localStorage` is empty; every created, edited, duplicated, and renamed resume vanishes on reload and the app resets to seeded demo data. Deletions also revert — a deleted seeded resume reappeared after reload. |\n| **FT-19** | **Date filtering not implemented.** The dashboard has exactly one input (text search) and no date picker, range control, or calendar of any kind. |\n| **CS-21** | **Whitespace title accepted via the dashboard rename dialog**, blanking the resume's name entirely. The editor path correctly reverts but gives no feedback either way. |\n| **CS-9** | **No date-period validation.** An end date before the start date, and dates years in the future (2030–2031), were both silently accepted and rendered in the preview. |\n| **CT-20** | **Minimal style omits the customized Summary heading.** The other three custom headings render, and Modern/Classic render all four — Minimal alone drops it. |\n\nTwo findings worth highlighting for triage priority: CS-11 undermines the product's central promise of *saving* multiple variations for different job applications, and CS-21's dashboard path is a genuine data-corrupting bug rather than a cosmetic one — it leaves a resume with no recoverable title on its card. I also noted that the editor and dashboard rename paths validate inconsistently, which suggests the validation lives in the editor component rather than in the shared rename logic."
  }
}
